Thank you - yes, biss-playwright-credentials in biss-cicd is a good name.

The secret needs two keys, named exactly like the files (the pipeline mounts the secret as a
folder, so each key becomes a file of that name):

  Key              Value
  db.properties    the contents of our db.properties file (Oracle test database connection)
  TestData.xlsx    the TestData.xlsx file (an Excel file, so it has to be added from the file)

Equivalent command:
  oc create secret generic biss-playwright-credentials -n biss-cicd \
     --from-file=db.properties=<path to db.properties> \
     --from-file=TestData.xlsx=<path to TestData.xlsx>

It does not need to be synced to Jenkins as a credential. The Jenkinsfile mounts it read-only
into the agent pod (podTemplate secretVolume, /home/jenkins/biss-secrets), the same way it
already uses mvn-repo-secret.

The two files contain passwords, so I will not attach them to this ticket. Please let me
know how you would like to receive them (screen-share, or another secure channel you prefer).

